CAPITALVEST — COMPLETE WEBSITE BUILD SPECIFICATION
Build a complete, premium, responsive, full-stack wealth management web application named CapitalVest.
Brand tagline: Building Wealth. Securing Generations.
Brand positioning: A modern wealth management command centre that helps financial advisors manage client relationships, monitor portfolios, track financial goals, evaluate financial health, identify risks, and generate professional financial reports. The platform should combine elegant client-facing experiences with powerful internal business operations.
This is not a static website, a simple dashboard mockup, or a landing-page-only project. Build an interconnected application with working navigation, real forms, realistic calculations, interactive charts, persistent records, secure authentication, data synchronization, and complete workflows.
1. Non-negotiable project requirements
1.	Build the entire application, from the public welcome page through authentication, onboarding, dashboards, every management module, settings, and logout.
2.	Prioritize Wealth Management Dashboard & Analytics and Excel/Spreadsheet Integration.
3.	Do not build, replace, activate, or modify an AI Advisor, Gemini chatbot, or other AI advisory feature in this version. Leave an appropriate future integration point in the architecture, but do not display a nonfunctional AI chat widget.
4.	Use Indian financial conventions, including INR (₹), Indian number formatting, DD/MM/YYYY dates, Indian names, and the Asia/Kolkata time zone.
5.	Use fictional demo clients and clearly label demo financial data as illustrative. Do not use real customer information.
6.	Use a real database and authentication. Do not pretend local browser state is a secure backend.
7.	Every visible button, link, filter, tab, form, search field, chart control, export option, and navigation item must work or be explicitly disabled with an explanation.
8.	Do not leave placeholder pages, empty navigation destinations, fake success messages, or unfinished sections.
9.	Build the complete application first. Then test all major flows, fix errors, and refine the visual design without removing functionality.
2. Technology stack and architecture
Use the following architecture unless a technical limitation requires an equivalent, clearly explained implementation.
•	Frontend: React, TypeScript, and a modern component-based architecture.
•	Styling: Tailwind CSS or an equivalent consistent styling system.
•	Icons: Lucide icons.
•	Charts: Recharts or another reliable React chart library.
•	Backend: Node.js server-side runtime with secure API endpoints.
•	Database: Firebase Cloud Firestore.
•	Authentication: Firebase Authentication, including Google Sign-In and email/password authentication where supported.
•	Spreadsheet integration: Google Sheets API or Google Workspace integration for live spreadsheet synchronization, plus an Excel .xlsx and .csv import workflow.
•	File processing: A suitable spreadsheet parsing library such as SheetJS.
•	PDF reports: A reliable PDF generation library.
•	Exports: CSV and Excel-compatible downloads.
•	Deployment: Ensure the application can be tested in AI Studio and prepared for deployment through its supported hosting workflow.
Keep data-access logic, business calculations, authentication, spreadsheet processing, and presentation components separate.
Store credentials and API secrets securely on the server. Never expose service-account credentials, private keys, or sensitive tokens in frontend code.
Use Firestore security rules and server-side authorization checks to enforce user roles and record access.
If Firebase setup is offered, configure it rather than silently substituting a local-only prototype. If a required external integration needs consent, credentials, or configuration, build the setup interface and clearly explain the remaining step.
