21. Core calculation and data integrity rules
Implement reusable calculation functions and test them.
•	Portfolio market value: calculate from valid quantities and prices, or use an explicitly defined valuation method for other asset types.
•	Total invested capital: calculate from available cost-basis or transaction data.
•	Unrealized gain/loss: market value minus the relevant cost basis.
•	Absolute return percentage: gain/loss divided by invested capital, where the denominator is valid.
•	Asset allocation: holding market value divided by total portfolio value.
•	Goal progress: current saved amount divided by target amount, with appropriate handling of zero targets and values above 100%.
•	Financial health: calculate using the documented, configurable scoring methodology.
•	Risk alerts: generate using stored values and configured thresholds.
•	Dashboard totals: derive from authorized, validated records.
•	Historical changes: compare equivalent date ranges only when valid historical snapshots are available.
Use decimal-safe financial calculations where appropriate. Format displayed INR values consistently.
Do not use hard-coded numbers to make charts appear functional. Charts and summary cards must derive from stored data or a clearly identified demo dataset.
When data is incomplete, show “Not available” or an equivalent explanatory state rather than silently inventing values.
